%% NMM (M, S) state lifecycle — when state is created, mutated, detached, reset, or discarded.
%% State refers to the per-layer recurrent (M, S) tuple maintained outside the model graph.

stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> Uninitialized: process start

    Uninitialized --> InitFromW: forward(idx, nmm_states=None)
    note right of InitFromW
        init_state(B, device):
        M = {W*: memory_mlp.W*.weight
                  .detach().clone()
                  .unsqueeze(0).expand(B,...)
                  .contiguous()}
        S = zeros_like(M)
        — G207: .to(device).clone() order
                avoids wasted source-device copy
    end note

    InitFromW --> Live: state ready

    Live --> Updating: per-token in forward_chunk
    note right of Updating
        Per token t (write-then-read):
          ℓ = ‖MLP(k̂; M_{t-1}) - v‖²
          g = vmap(grad(...))(M, k̂, v)
          g̃ = NS5(g)               (fp32, autocast off)
          S = η·S - θ·g̃            (θ POST-NS)
          M = (1-α)·M + S
          y = out_scale ⊙ MLP(q̂; M_t)
    end note
    Updating --> Live: chunk forward complete

    Live --> ResetOnDoc: doc_boundaries[b,t] == True
    note left of ResetOnDoc
        torch.where(mask[..., None, None],
                    init_M, M)
        — NOT in-place assignment
        (autograd tensor → RuntimeError)
        Lazy-build init_M only when a
        boundary actually fires (G211)
    end note
    ResetOnDoc --> Live

    Live --> NaNDetected: loss / state non-finite
    note right of NaNDetected
        Caught in train_step:
          if not torch.isfinite(loss):
              optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)
              return (loss, None, None)
        Caller MUST reset nmm_states=None.
        DDP accumulation path ALSO resets
        (G213, G217) — otherwise corrupt
        state persists across micro-batches.
    end note
    NaNDetected --> Uninitialized: nmm_states := None
    Uninitialized --> InitFromW: next forward rebuilds

    Live --> Detached: between TBPTT chunks
    note left of Detached
        detach_states(states):
          for each leaf in nested (M, S):
              t.detach()
          handles state=None (G149)
        Cuts the autograd graph so the
        next chunk's backward doesn't
        reach into the previous chunk.
        Values are preserved; only the
        graph link is severed.
    end note
    Detached --> Live: next chunk begins<br/>(same (M, S) values, fresh graph)

    Live --> DiscardedOnRankBoundary: end of micro-batch in DDP
    note right of DiscardedOnRankBoundary
        nmm_states do NOT cross ranks.
        Each rank maintains its own.
        At optimizer.step() the values
        are retained for the next batch,
        but the graph is fully detached.
    end note
    DiscardedOnRankBoundary --> Live

    Live --> NotSavedToCheckpoint: ckpt_save fires
    note left of NotSavedToCheckpoint
        nmm_states are NOT in the
        checkpoint dict. Per-sequence
        recurrent state, not model state.
        save({'model': ..., 'optimizer': ...,
              'scheduler': ..., 'step': ...})
    end note
    NotSavedToCheckpoint --> Live

    Live --> Uninitialized: process resume from checkpoint
    note right of Uninitialized
        On resume:
          1. Build model
          2. load_state_dict
          3. wrap DDP
          4. build optimizer
          5. load_optimizer (if present)
          6. model.train()
        → nmm_states starts as None;
          first forward triggers InitFromW
          from the (possibly trained)
          memory_mlp.W*.weight values.
    end note

    Live --> [*]: process exit
    NaNDetected --> [*]: unrecoverable<br/>(params went NaN, not just state)
